{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:29:02.677531Z","id":"d88c494d3513db1a632f557999ffaf761fc8afcb82d75afeb55a3b9b9a8cba32","body":{"detail":"frameLoaded() closes the gate on a load with no hello, calls leaveDocument() (host.leave()), and asks the page to greet again with clax:greet. The page's hello reopens the gate, but the capability host starts over, so everything the page had set up through it ends and the page must set it up again. The spec states this as an open limitation (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-28-clax-design.md:1167-1171).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":640},"end":{"line":658},"content_hash":"72305be614779699d14d6ef0e341ca8695bf7df61efd86ed49f766a51dfdd6f9"},"suggested_fix":"When the hello that answers clax:greet comes from the same document (same artifact, version and file), keep or re-establish the host's room joins, db subscriptions, sample streams and custom anchors instead of starting over.","summary":"Back or Forward across a page's own fragments drops its room joins, db subscriptions, sample streams and custom anchors","supersedes":"7bec3684a53d4d228891f147137a443ef36e11d906cba05a2696681207c4cf0e","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:29:02.679052Z","id":"a5cb81392a1820e92cfaeccb56c65b09795db8d6268970381eeb6524caea4081","body":{"detail":"After clax:degraded, the shell holds the part failed for that page: Comment stays off and says so, even once the bridge's own retry could load the part, and threads whose anchors went unanswered while it failed stay unplaced. This needs a protocol addition.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1258},"end":{"line":1268},"content_hash":"d916958d7195a5a877a49f0b9d1b6e048afccef5dc947da03e0bf784247f5cbe"},"suggested_fix":"Have the bridge report a part that loads after failing; the shell then clears failedParts for it and its notice, and resolves the anchors again.","summary":"A lazy part that failed stays failed until the page's next hello, even once it loads","supersedes":"76a00f1b49d5b22fa1e7deb61eece0b7ae52086b335bcdb05f2bc760a5b46906","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:29:02.680557Z","id":"4c619de2339b6691067f2b39aba627e5e0005ff3e62b038ff32d6139b2c09305","body":{"detail":"A page's own publish (artifact.publish) moves every open unpinned view to the new version when the view hears its version event, which carries by_page (lines 115-128). A view whose stream goes live only after that publish learns of the version from this refetch on ready, which cannot tell who published, and offers Reload in the top bar. The browser tests wait for each view's stream before a vote (streamLive in web/e2e/fixtures.ts:203).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":165},"end":{"line":170},"content_hash":"a91a85289e6e1f0f950c25198984f37c048a7650c830e9460e903fe262484c32"},"summary":"A view that missed a page's publish offers Reload rather than following it","supersedes":"69abb375e48b9757b02124e6d05bf820e28c661a3a33cc98d15d34112f5cfbd5","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:49.657088Z","id":"ca4f03a0344e7c87739d57d46c4437c39bc570ca84dbaa9a3e0371ee4b48085e","body":{"detail":"After clax:degraded, the shell holds the part failed for that page: Comment stays off and says so, even once the bridge's own retry could load the part, and threads whose anchors went unanswered while it failed stay unplaced. This needs a protocol addition.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1260},"end":{"line":1270},"content_hash":"d916958d7195a5a877a49f0b9d1b6e048afccef5dc947da03e0bf784247f5cbe"},"suggested_fix":"Have the bridge report a part that loads after failing; the shell then clears failedParts for it and its notice, and resolves the anchors again.","summary":"A lazy part that failed stays failed until the page's next hello, even once it loads","supersedes":"a5cb81392a1820e92cfaeccb56c65b09795db8d6268970381eeb6524caea4081","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:34:08.581288Z","id":"e39ce82c8bfab9f40e583dafd2ecbdf53d49a55c5b5059e94f6af5498e90baf2","body":{"detail":"A spectator has no live topics, so its stream carries no `drafts` events, and the snapshot it polls (crates/clax-server/src/routes/snapshot.rs, built as Caller::Anonymous and shared between viewers) carries no drafts, since drafts reach named people only. A connected person who is a spectator gets the list from GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/drafts when the view loads; a draft revised or ended after that is not reflected until the person joins live or reloads. Shown with Show draft, an ended draft's URL answers 404.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1516},"end":{"line":1520},"content_hash":"9e4706af13fc12edd7d3c958d4b1693d8fb21bc378690685435dcc04e64ecf9e"},"summary":"A spectator's draft banner shows the drafts listed at load and does not follow them","tags":["drafts","seats","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:23:02.671359Z","id":"37ab4938a7b13f4b72a909b416d8ae3249022c319159acaf1b96801b90c4b43e","body":{"detail":"Both come from the content frame's window, where the artifact's scripts run beside the bridge, and the shell cannot tell the bridge's post from the page's. A page can so show others a pointer or selection the viewer did not make, and place the tags of the people present (only keys the shell gave this document, only their names) anywhere over its own frame. Neither reaches anything outside the frame's box or any name the shell did not already show; the same holds of the hosted prototype's content script (hosted/src/content-selection.ts).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1278},"end":{"line":1281},"content_hash":"bd25d785eecf30fcdb267bfa3b6ac7352f73a5bc78797a7beac0aec43d8158a2"},"summary":"The page itself can post clax:cursor and clax:peer-at, so it can move this viewer's pointer as others see it, and the name tags over its frame","tags":["live-layers","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:16:01.906751Z","id":"f1cd616bd0b2093bedffc6bd841dc65ba75d823b6dc5680f9761e7af8cf1dd44","body":{"detail":"frameLoaded() closes the gate on a load with no hello, calls leaveDocument() (host.leave()), and asks the page to greet again with clax:greet. The page's hello reopens the gate, but the capability host starts over, so everything the page had set up through it ends and the page must set it up again. The spec states this as an open limitation (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-28-clax-design.md:1167-1171).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":629},"end":{"line":647},"content_hash":"72305be614779699d14d6ef0e341ca8695bf7df61efd86ed49f766a51dfdd6f9"},"suggested_fix":"When the hello that answers clax:greet comes from the same document (same artifact, version and file), keep or re-establish the host's room joins, db subscriptions, sample streams and custom anchors instead of starting over.","summary":"Back or Forward across a page's own fragments drops its room joins, db subscriptions, sample streams and custom anchors","supersedes":"7bec3684a53d4d228891f147137a443ef36e11d906cba05a2696681207c4cf0e","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:16:01.908234Z","id":"b00fa546fb4dd1c257d99f8384e5ba4fb8dc11adcc0e08ccde452d46dccdefc0","body":{"detail":"After clax:degraded, the shell holds the part failed for that page: Comment stays off and says so, even once the bridge's own retry could load the part, and threads whose anchors went unanswered while it failed stay unplaced. This needs a protocol addition.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1259},"end":{"line":1270},"content_hash":"a62726f22b968223e5a0600a02409de464b16b80a863c60f4f5a0f057e2bb465"},"suggested_fix":"Have the bridge report a part that loads after failing; the shell then clears failedParts for it and its notice, and resolves the anchors again.","summary":"A lazy part that failed stays failed until the page's next hello, even once it loads","supersedes":"76a00f1b49d5b22fa1e7deb61eece0b7ae52086b335bcdb05f2bc760a5b46906","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:16:01.909701Z","id":"083a554ed5107ec86e84e9790e68b262f5916f5ff2e5fb9fcb175a1324c3e7b2","body":{"detail":"Both come from the content frame's window, where the artifact's scripts run beside the bridge, and the shell cannot tell the bridge's post from the page's. A page can so show others a pointer, selection or pick the viewer did not make, and place the tags of the people present (only keys the shell gave this document, only their names) anywhere over its own frame. Neither reaches anything outside the frame's box or any name the shell did not already show, and it cannot speak as anyone but its own viewer: the daemon keys every live message by the socket's person (crates/clax-server/src/live_layers.rs apply). Whatever the page posts, the shell sends the cursor at most every LIVE_CURSOR_MS (web/shell/src/view/live-view.ts sendCursor), so a page cannot push its viewer's socket over the daemon's rate and have it closed 1008. What the frame learns of others: their pointers and selections, an opaque key and colour each (the colour is the person's ID's FNV-1a hash mod 8 while that colour is free), and through clax:peers' `here` whether anyone else is on the artifact; never a name or an ID. The same holds of the hosted prototype's content script (hosted/src/content-selection.ts).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1272},"end":{"line":1275},"content_hash":"bd25d785eecf30fcdb267bfa3b6ac7352f73a5bc78797a7beac0aec43d8158a2"},"summary":"The page itself can post clax:cursor and clax:peer-at, so it can move this viewer's pointer, selection and pick as others see them, and the name tags over its frame","supersedes":"37ab4938a7b13f4b72a909b416d8ae3249022c319159acaf1b96801b90c4b43e","tags":["live-layers","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/live-layers.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:16:01.912775Z","id":"f19b03bb34d3bc3d554c51c76300eb1518b5b2c6bac3975d99a6933fa4cf02bd","body":{"detail":"Both put their text under thread null (web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts composerInput, web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte NewComment onText), and DraftSender keys boxes by thread ID, null as \"\": typing in one replaces the other's draft as others see it, and the Composer's onDestroy (web/shell/src/ui/Composer.svelte onText(\"\")) clears the shared key, so the box still open shows no draft to others until its next keystroke.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":228},"end":{"line":229},"content_hash":"1e865cb799cd24e5af73e16cf362d1a3dce94df91faba77af866c04bd9b0a84d"},"suggested_fix":"Key the pick composer's draft apart from the whole-artifact box (a draft kind or a box ID in the live message), or send the remaining box's text again when the other closes.","summary":"The pick composer and the New comment box share one live draft, so with both open each overwrites the other's and closing one ends both","tags":["live-layers","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:32:12.236045Z","id":"081d67b95632beccca141b41381700dfaa0e3bbe1320971e4b13af61163aa133","body":{"detail":"frameLoaded() closes the gate on a load with no hello, calls leaveDocument() (host.leave()), and asks the page to greet again with clax:greet. The page's hello reopens the gate, but the capability host starts over, so everything the page had set up through it ends and the page must set it up again. The spec states this as an open limitation (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-28-clax-design.md:1167-1171).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":657},"end":{"line":675},"content_hash":"72305be614779699d14d6ef0e341ca8695bf7df61efd86ed49f766a51dfdd6f9"},"suggested_fix":"When the hello that answers clax:greet comes from the same document (same artifact, version and file), keep or re-establish the host's room joins, db subscriptions, sample streams and custom anchors instead of starting over.","summary":"Back or Forward across a page's own fragments drops its room joins, db subscriptions, sample streams and custom anchors","supersedes":"f1cd616bd0b2093bedffc6bd841dc65ba75d823b6dc5680f9761e7af8cf1dd44","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:32:12.238741Z","id":"73d711820ba7cddf3791590414fb049a40f728e1ada5044296f034db9f170daa","body":{"detail":"After clax:degraded, the shell holds the part failed for that page: Comment stays off and says so, even once the bridge's own retry could load the part, and threads whose anchors went unanswered while it failed stay unplaced. This needs a protocol addition.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1292},"end":{"line":1303},"content_hash":"a62726f22b968223e5a0600a02409de464b16b80a863c60f4f5a0f057e2bb465"},"suggested_fix":"Have the bridge report a part that loads after failing; the shell then clears failedParts for it and its notice, and resolves the anchors again.","summary":"A lazy part that failed stays failed until the page's next hello, even once it loads","supersedes":"b00fa546fb4dd1c257d99f8384e5ba4fb8dc11adcc0e08ccde452d46dccdefc0","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:32:12.241209Z","id":"51221196911aaf34eb3f469cf074891b845dcd459e7924be424fc8a981c9a0e5","body":{"detail":"Both come from the content frame's window, where the artifact's scripts run beside the bridge, and the shell cannot tell the bridge's post from the page's. A page can so show others a pointer, selection or pick the viewer did not make, and place the tags of the people present (only keys the shell gave this document, only their names) anywhere over its own frame. Neither reaches anything outside the frame's box or any name the shell did not already show, and it cannot speak as anyone but its own viewer: the daemon keys every live message by the socket's person (crates/clax-server/src/live_layers.rs apply). Whatever the page posts, the shell sends the cursor at most every LIVE_CURSOR_MS (web/shell/src/view/live-view.ts sendCursor), so a page cannot push its viewer's socket over the daemon's rate and have it closed 1008. What the frame learns of others: their pointers and selections, an opaque key and colour each (the colour is the person's ID's FNV-1a hash mod 8 while that colour is free), and through clax:peers' `here` whether anyone else is on the artifact; never a name or an ID. The same holds of the hosted prototype's content script (hosted/src/content-selection.ts).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1305},"end":{"line":1308},"content_hash":"bd25d785eecf30fcdb267bfa3b6ac7352f73a5bc78797a7beac0aec43d8158a2"},"summary":"The page itself can post clax:cursor and clax:peer-at, so it can move this viewer's pointer, selection and pick as others see them, and the name tags over its frame","supersedes":"083a554ed5107ec86e84e9790e68b262f5916f5ff2e5fb9fcb175a1324c3e7b2","tags":["live-layers","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:32:12.243658Z","id":"08ca7f94c20befbf47443b4916ab2b7998afcc5e455fd32496f115c77c82a64a","body":{"detail":"A spectator has no live topics, so its stream carries no `drafts` events, and the snapshot it polls (crates/clax-server/src/routes/snapshot.rs, built as Caller::Anonymous and shared between viewers) carries no drafts, since drafts reach named people only. A connected person who is a spectator gets the list from GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/drafts when the view loads; a draft revised or ended after that is not reflected until the person joins live or reloads. Shown with Show draft, an ended draft's URL answers 404.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1500},"end":{"line":1504},"content_hash":"9e4706af13fc12edd7d3c958d4b1693d8fb21bc378690685435dcc04e64ecf9e"},"summary":"A spectator's draft banner shows the drafts listed at load and does not follow them","supersedes":"e39ce82c8bfab9f40e583dafd2ecbdf53d49a55c5b5059e94f6af5498e90baf2","tags":["drafts","seats","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/spectator.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:32:12.246230Z","id":"5b716bd53a41a4b163aff41bdb9499f93a144fb698ae7f34660cab18d312f40c","body":{"detail":"joinOffered reads seats_free or guest_seats_free from the shared snapshot, which counts the pool only. A person refused a seat who then gets rights naming the artifact by ID would get a reserved seat on Join live, but the banner offers it only once a pool seat is free (or after a reload).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":58},"end":{"line":61},"content_hash":"9a1e7ab58a77ff4dfb10b30f33ec302944bad666c6312a0ca89bc2e1080f6755"},"summary":"A spectator who is granted a share is not offered Join live until a pool seat frees","supersedes":"1e04877cafbc8b563db669466e813604042b3d6469f06f4f60811a3f9e40fe2c","tags":["live-seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/presence-reporter.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:32:12.248900Z","id":"9312bc41777c6a27bc8108f4a3babd35d735d5b7985b0f06b8243c0c8d511605","body":{"detail":"The count comes from PUT and GET presence answers (and a spectator's snapshot); presence events do not carry it, and spectators come and go without one. A seated viewer's count is refreshed by the 30 s heartbeat, so it may lag by that much.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":41},"end":{"line":41},"content_hash":"d1005b8c07998c933d8f91cbe85fc38eeab6e0221557c88d17940a089ae0cd0a"},"summary":"A seated viewer's 'N viewing' count follows only their own presence reports","supersedes":"644b88d20216a1b1935195487e1bec1a4e05b262e0c47319055f6a3cafab6272","tags":["live-seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.083514Z","id":"f988167d55aaafd37169305a9378e67215cb330e1c23691cd78164ef25fdd3f5","body":{"detail":"frameLoaded() closes the gate on a load with no hello, calls leaveDocument() (host.leave()), and asks the page to greet again with clax:greet. The page's hello reopens the gate, but the capability host starts over, so everything the page had set up through it ends and the page must set it up again. The spec states this as an open limitation (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-28-clax-design.md:1167-1171).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":643},"end":{"line":661},"content_hash":"72305be614779699d14d6ef0e341ca8695bf7df61efd86ed49f766a51dfdd6f9"},"suggested_fix":"When the hello that answers clax:greet comes from the same document (same artifact, version and file), keep or re-establish the host's room joins, db subscriptions, sample streams and custom anchors instead of starting over.","summary":"Back or Forward across a page's own fragments drops its room joins, db subscriptions, sample streams and custom anchors","supersedes":"809b2f2f54598dc6eb9ce4f394f16eca0823f043eaa7c700ce2d0da4781617d7","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
